{"kind":"request","text":"Design note: a member with a publisher role writes to the Git host, and the scope never sends to an outside system.\n\nFiled 2026-11-13 13:02 EST at Hugh's request, from a design review session beside the main planner session. Hugh's words on the route: \"yes this seems worthwhile, please draft a design-note and send to the main planner session to progress through review\". Every dap fact below is read at main `64112e45`.\n\n## Outcome\n\nAn application gets an effect on an outside system with forms that it already has: slots, acts, guards and a member. The kernel's four operation forms stop at one family and can later leave.\n\n## Why\n\nGit publication is the one place where a scope itself sends. For it the kernel carries the effects `operation` and `attempt` and the inputs `outcome` and `preparation`: 4,205 lines of `packages/derive` and 4,118 lines of `packages/scope` by `wc -l` over the files that the note lists, and 35 `P16` marks in `packages/platform` by `grep`. One shelf page of the lending library reserves up to eighteen outside operations in the destination. A declared application cannot declare an operation of its own.\n\ndap already takes the member route in four places: the checker service, `device-command@1`, a room with host `none`, and the text of a shelf page.\n\n## What draft 1 decides\n\n1. A scope never sends to an outside system. A member does the work and signs an act that states the result.\n2. A publication is a fold of the journal that a member runs. The record keeps the published commit and the last entry that the commit covers.\n3. A lost answer stays outside the record. The publisher reads the branch before it signs, so the record holds no `unknown` result.\n4. The record uses declared forms only: four slots and four acts on one item. The kernel gains nothing.\n5. The first version (slice P1) publishes the lending library's shelf pages in a room with host `none`, with eight witnesses and no network.\n\nThe note lists five questions for the room's change publication and designs none of them. One of them waits for the note that sizes several definitions in one scope.\n\n## Draft\n\nPath `notes/2026-11-13-publisher-member.md`, draft 1, on branch `planner/publisher-member-20261113`, in worktree `~/play/artroom-worktrees/planner-publisher-member-20261113`. The head is one commit on main `64112e45`. The head changes that one file. `node scripts/check-doc-links.mjs` and `git diff --check` pass. No gate ran.\n\n## Decisions for Hugh at ratification\n\n1. Who runs a hosted publisher and holds its Git credential: the operator, the room's owner, or either (note section 7).\n2. Whether slice P1 runs inside the stable base of order `fc7576f8` or after it. P1 changes only `examples/lending`.\n\nThe decisions on kernel promises 2 and 11 belong to slice P4 and are not asked now.\n\n## Kernel filing rule\n\nThe note adds no scope kind, platform definition name, capability, tool family or record model. It names K1 and K4 as the items that later slices serve, and it states that slice P1 closes neither.","body":{"conditions":"The note notes/2026-11-13-publisher-member.md lands on main with its status line, after the checker approves the head and Hugh ratifies the note. The head changes only that file. The note adds no scope kind, definition name, capability, tool family or record model, or it names the K item. After the landing, the planner files slice P1 as a child request to the builder, with the eight witnesses of section 12.","target_head":"64112e4576b4c3c8fb668389786deb6b703da417","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}